WEBVTT

00:11.928 --> 00:14.305
You finally come.

00:14.389 --> 00:18.143
Well, I'm not going to
complain about that.

00:18.226 --> 00:20.520
I'm the one who called you, after all.

00:21.688 --> 00:24.524
So, since you came…

00:25.108 --> 00:29.821
Should I assume that you're
willing to bargain with me?

00:32.073 --> 00:34.117
Arthur Pencilgon-san.

00:40.540 --> 00:43.918
(Red or Green?)
I want to always stay incomplete Yeah

00:44.002 --> 00:47.380
(Red or Green?)
Lalala Red Light? Green Light?

00:47.464 --> 00:50.759
(Red or Green?)
No, not yet This is not my limit Yeah

00:50.842 --> 00:54.304
(Red or Green?)
Lalala Red Light? Green Light?

01:01.144 --> 01:04.522
I even miss the scar now

01:04.606 --> 01:07.317
It's not sparkling, it's glaring

01:07.400 --> 01:08.985
(Chase me! Chase me!)

01:09.069 --> 01:11.362
Even when I catch you

01:11.446 --> 01:14.783
Your robe simply swings

01:14.866 --> 01:17.494
Be it love or hate, it's all the same

01:17.577 --> 01:20.997
They'll be nutrition once I swallow them

01:21.081 --> 01:24.459
It's a great answer that
even shines the uncertain truth

01:24.542 --> 01:27.962
I will bloom profusely over and over

01:28.046 --> 01:31.925
Moonlight
Split the cloud, show me your face

01:32.008 --> 01:34.677
(Let's dance lala lalala)

01:34.761 --> 01:38.890
Tonight
Light up the darkness and make a sound

01:38.973 --> 01:41.476
(Let's dance A lonely dance)

01:41.559 --> 01:45.647
I want to keep it all to myself,
loving it completely

01:45.730 --> 01:49.692
I have no more doubts in me
Oh Yeah!

01:49.776 --> 01:52.529
I won't give this away, I am the QUEEN

01:52.612 --> 01:56.032
I will not be satisfied,
I will not be disturbed Yeah

02:02.872 --> 02:06.668
(Red or Green?)
I have no limit Yeah

02:10.797 --> 02:15.510
First, I'll break those
supporting columns!

02:15.593 --> 02:20.598
With these on, I wonder how much more
damage I'll deal using that skill combo!

02:20.682 --> 02:23.017
Let's go, Gilta Brille!

02:23.101 --> 02:23.935
(Infight)

02:24.018 --> 02:26.521
Going from Infight…

02:26.604 --> 02:28.731
…to Hand of Fortune!

02:28.815 --> 02:31.025
(Hand of Fortune)

02:34.279 --> 02:36.614
Break!

02:40.451 --> 02:42.745
Woohoo! One-hit break!

02:43.955 --> 02:45.748
The first column down!

02:45.832 --> 02:48.167
Next! The second one!

02:51.671 --> 02:54.048
My Shana-oh Possession wore off.

02:56.259 --> 02:59.721
I doubt I can reach
the other side without a buff.

03:02.140 --> 03:04.809
<i>It'll take twenty seconds if</i>
<i>I go from the rubble below.</i>

03:04.893 --> 03:07.645
<i>I can't break a minute, then…</i>

03:08.479 --> 03:10.565
<i>Divinity tech…</i>

03:12.025 --> 03:14.277
<i>I read the description…</i>

03:14.360 --> 03:17.155
…but looks like I just gotta
give it a try on the fly!

03:18.781 --> 03:20.283
Firing up!

03:22.660 --> 03:27.874
First of the several voice-activated
commands, Crystal Bullet!

03:29.125 --> 03:30.919
And the second is…

03:31.002 --> 03:32.587
Growing-up!

03:34.547 --> 03:37.467
After detecting a certain
vibration wavelength,

03:37.550 --> 03:40.094
the Crystal Bullet will
begin to rapidly grow!

03:42.305 --> 03:45.725
Haha! That's a Legacy Weapon for you!

03:45.808 --> 03:49.854
It got more than just attack force!
It's the greatest toy ever!

03:49.938 --> 03:51.064
Landing!

03:51.147 --> 03:52.690
Thirteen seconds left!

03:52.774 --> 03:56.653
I can't wait for Hand of Fortune
to finish recharging!

03:56.736 --> 04:01.532
I'll show you my Quick-Draw Fist
I honed over in <i>BERP</i>!

04:12.085 --> 04:14.796
I can't get taken down
after coming this far!

04:14.879 --> 04:18.174
Time to seal this off with a slam dunk!

04:22.595 --> 04:23.429
(Fleet Float)

04:34.941 --> 04:37.527
It instantly dies after getting
its core crushed by the weight.

04:38.444 --> 04:41.447
I can't believe just hitting the
wheel would kill it just like that.

04:41.531 --> 04:45.952
Quite a lame way to go for a
boss in the second-half content.

04:47.036 --> 04:48.955
But either way…

04:49.038 --> 04:51.708
I took it down in 59 seconds!

04:51.791 --> 04:55.837
Woohoo! A brand-new record for a solo run!

04:55.920 --> 05:00.049
This Gilta Brille's Crystal Bullet
seems to have a lot of use

05:00.133 --> 05:03.219
and there's still some nasty stuff
I haven't used yet.

05:03.303 --> 05:05.555
This ought to be a lot of fun!

05:08.516 --> 05:12.395
No mere Area Boss can
stop me in my conquest!

05:14.897 --> 05:19.652
(Leventar)

05:19.736 --> 05:21.821
Whoa!

05:21.904 --> 05:24.157
It's got 400 vitality!

05:24.240 --> 05:26.409
It looks great on you!

05:26.492 --> 05:31.664
This sash alone is enough for
the requirement to use Gilta Brille!

05:31.748 --> 05:33.708
Still, even though this is just a sash,

05:33.791 --> 05:39.005
the Spiked Battlehelm [4A]
I made early on still gives more VIT.

05:40.006 --> 05:43.926
Between this and Gila Brille,
Beelach-made stuff sure is special.

05:44.010 --> 05:46.095
Thank you for your patronage!

05:48.056 --> 05:52.727
So, I still have a little more time
before my meet-up with Psyger-0.

05:52.810 --> 05:54.771
Psyger-0 looked super pissed,
weren't they?

05:54.854 --> 05:55.688
Huh?

05:55.772 --> 05:58.191
Yeah, that intimidating aura was no joke.

05:58.274 --> 06:01.069
They're not called
"Attack Master" for nothing.

06:01.152 --> 06:04.655
I wonder who they're
waiting for so long.

06:04.739 --> 06:09.202
We saw them there an hour ago, so
whoever it is, they must hate them a lot.

06:09.285 --> 06:13.539
You think they'd slash whoever
that person is in half on sight?

06:13.623 --> 06:16.209
My condolences to that poor person, then.

06:16.292 --> 06:21.214
<i>Huh?! Did I get our meet-up time wrong?!</i>

06:21.297 --> 06:23.299
<i>Now's not the time for shopping!</i>

06:25.718 --> 06:27.553
I'm truly sorry!

06:28.304 --> 06:30.765
Huh?! Wha-, Sunraku-san?!

06:30.848 --> 06:34.894
Looks like I made you wait for
so long. I have no words to say.

06:35.478 --> 06:40.817
No, no, no, no!
I came early, that's all!

06:40.900 --> 06:42.777
Please, raise your head.

06:45.488 --> 06:49.492
Um, I just happen to have
some free time, so…

06:49.575 --> 06:51.494
It's no problem… at all.

06:52.453 --> 06:55.414
<i>They don't seem to be mad.</i>
<i>Thank goodness.</i>

06:55.498 --> 06:56.541
Des.

06:56.624 --> 06:58.334
<i>Death?!</i>

06:58.876 --> 07:01.003
<i>They're mad after all!</i>

07:01.087 --> 07:04.298
Uh, so, it's no… problem?

07:04.382 --> 07:06.884
<i>Phew. I was freaked out.</i>

07:07.510 --> 07:11.139
<i>For a second there I thought</i>
<i>Schwarz Vulf had some weird rule</i>

07:11.222 --> 07:15.143
<i>about meeting an hour</i>
<i>in advance or something.</i>

07:16.144 --> 07:18.646
Okay, so, Psyger-0.

07:18.729 --> 07:20.231
Y-Yes?

07:20.314 --> 07:25.319
I was hoping you could help me
beat the Lightless Barrens.

07:25.403 --> 07:28.114
What reward would you like for your time?

07:28.197 --> 07:30.324
Oh no, I don't need anything!

07:30.408 --> 07:32.034
Huh? But…

07:32.118 --> 07:35.913
I mean, we… we're friends, aren't we?

07:35.997 --> 07:37.665
No need to worry about it.

07:38.416 --> 07:39.834
Huh…

07:39.917 --> 07:43.921
<i>My mission today is to give</i>
<i>Hizutome-kun a good impression</i>

07:44.005 --> 07:45.715
<i>and close the distance between us!</i>

07:45.798 --> 07:47.550
<i>And to do that…</i>

07:49.427 --> 07:52.430
I'll help you out with anything
you need, free of charge!

07:55.433 --> 07:59.604
<i>Free charity is the scariest</i>
<i>thing of all, though!</i>

07:59.687 --> 08:03.357
<i>What is it… What are</i>
<i>you thinking, Psyger-0!</i>

08:03.441 --> 08:06.569
Well then, let's get it going right away!

08:06.652 --> 08:07.653
O-Okay!

08:10.615 --> 08:14.869
This area, much like
the Ruins of Past Glories before it,

08:14.952 --> 08:18.247
is a place that strongly evokes
the Divinity civilization,

08:18.331 --> 08:21.125
but unlike the ruins
which were a factory site,

08:21.209 --> 08:24.045
this place is the site of a battlefield.

08:24.670 --> 08:29.842
Looks like it must've been a pretty
intense fight, here in Lightless Barrens.

08:29.926 --> 08:35.848
(Lightless Barrens)

08:35.932 --> 08:39.852
Is that some kind of giant arm?

08:39.936 --> 08:43.397
According to the members of the Library,

08:43.481 --> 08:46.817
a large-scale battle, where
the army was pushed all the way

08:46.901 --> 08:50.363
back to the weapon factories,
took place here.

08:50.446 --> 08:53.407
Between this and the
spine-thing over on the road

08:53.491 --> 08:56.369
how enormous were the guys in this fight?

08:56.452 --> 09:01.707
Monsters of that size
have yet to be found in <i>SLF</i>.

09:02.583 --> 09:08.756
The Library was apparently founded in part
to figure out what happened in the past.

09:10.758 --> 09:14.303
<i>That projection of monster</i>
<i>I found in that underground lab…</i>

09:16.138 --> 09:21.561
<i>Is it connected to this</i>
<i>giant arm or that spine?</i>

09:21.644 --> 09:25.231
<i>If you want to find your own roots…</i>

09:25.314 --> 09:28.651
<i>The truth behind the world…</i>

09:28.734 --> 09:30.778
<i>You must search for Bahamut.</i>

09:31.737 --> 09:35.157
<i>None of the information</i>
<i>seems to be connected directly,</i>

09:35.241 --> 09:38.119
<i>but there's got to be something</i>
<i>that connects it all.</i>

09:38.202 --> 09:43.082
<i>And the key is likely</i>
<i>the EX Unique Scenarios.</i>

09:43.165 --> 09:44.584
<i>In other words,</i>

09:44.667 --> 09:49.380
<i>"If you want to know, go beat the Unique</i>
<i>Monsters," is what they're saying, right?</i>

09:49.463 --> 09:50.298
Huh?

09:50.381 --> 09:52.675
Oh, um, nevermind.

09:54.885 --> 09:58.431
U-Um, Sunraku-san.

09:58.514 --> 09:59.348
Yes?

09:59.640 --> 10:06.647
You told me your priority is to beat this
area and reach Fifticia by tomorrow…

10:07.440 --> 10:13.946
Is it… um… for a meet-up with someone?

10:15.781 --> 10:21.370
Uh, it's with two players
I met in another game, though.

10:21.454 --> 10:25.374
Um, well, could it be that…

10:25.458 --> 10:29.378
…these two players are… women?

10:29.462 --> 10:31.589
Well, one of them, yeah.

10:33.132 --> 10:34.258
Behind you!

10:47.938 --> 10:49.857
This woman…

10:50.608 --> 10:54.779
Is she your friend… as well?

10:56.614 --> 10:58.866
Uuuh…

11:00.159 --> 11:03.412
We haven't met in <i>SLF</i>…

11:03.496 --> 11:05.790
So she's not on my friend list yet…

11:05.873 --> 11:08.918
She's not your friend… yet!

11:09.001 --> 11:12.671
<i>That means maybe I still have a chance!</i>

11:12.755 --> 11:16.884
But that one-hit kill was impressive!
Did you apply some buff?

11:17.426 --> 11:19.887
<i>Before we reach Fifticia…</i>

11:21.263 --> 11:24.517
<i>As we beat the Lightless Barrens…</i>

11:25.518 --> 11:29.271
<i>…I will close the distance</i>
<i>between me and Hizutome-kun!</i>

11:30.898 --> 11:34.193
<i>They really emit some intimidating aura…</i>

11:34.735 --> 11:37.196
<i>I know I'm the one asking for help here…</i>

11:37.279 --> 11:40.032
<i>…but part of me kinda wants</i>
<i>to go back to Rabituza.</i>

11:40.116 --> 11:41.492
What's wrong?

11:41.575 --> 11:44.078
Sunraku-san, do you not feel well?

11:44.161 --> 11:46.372
N-No! I'm fine!

11:46.455 --> 11:48.624
Let's get going, Psyger-0!

11:48.707 --> 11:49.542
Right!

11:49.625 --> 11:51.585
I'll slash anything that comes our way!

11:51.669 --> 11:54.547
Th-That's reassuring to hear.

12:02.847 --> 12:04.640
Supreme Slash!

12:05.349 --> 12:07.059
(Supreme Slash)

12:11.897 --> 12:14.692
Whoa! Good one, Psyger-0!

12:14.775 --> 12:16.819
You slashed through its sturdy
outer shell like paper!

12:16.902 --> 12:22.575
No, no! You attracted its attention
so I was able to focus on attacking!

12:22.658 --> 12:26.245
We've fought a fair number
of monsters up to now,

12:26.328 --> 12:30.207
but you haven't taken a single hit!
It's amazing!

12:30.291 --> 12:33.002
I'll die even from
a single hit, after all.

12:33.085 --> 12:35.921
Because of this Mark,
as you can see, I'm half-naked.

12:36.547 --> 12:40.551
<i>That's right! Sunraku-san</i>
<i>is half-naked right now!</i>

12:41.135 --> 12:48.058
Th-Then, we better get that Mark removed
so you can equip proper armor!

12:48.726 --> 12:52.188
That's right, but I'm actually
kinda wavering on that.

12:53.272 --> 12:57.151
I've actually been helped on
occasion by this Mark's effect.

12:57.818 --> 13:01.447
But if possible, I'd like to at least
dispel it off my legs, maybe.

13:01.530 --> 13:04.325
If I remember right,
according to Psyger-100,

13:04.408 --> 13:07.411
I can have this NPC Eristella
help me out with it?

13:07.953 --> 13:13.501
She's a unique NPC, the only one in
<i>SLF</i> who can undo all types of curses.

13:13.584 --> 13:18.422
I believe she can remove
even Lycagon's Mark.

13:19.298 --> 13:22.426
But Saint Eristella is extremely popular,

13:22.510 --> 13:24.845
where she's not only
guarded by NPCs in the church,

13:24.929 --> 13:28.307
but also by
lots of high-level players,

13:28.390 --> 13:30.476
making it hard to even meet her.

13:30.559 --> 13:33.270
Her loyal fanbase, huh.

13:33.354 --> 13:35.105
Sounds like a group
one shouldn't mess with.

13:35.189 --> 13:41.278
And although normally it'd cost a fortune
and strong connections to meet her,

13:41.362 --> 13:45.366
but with help from Psyger-100
the leader of the Schwarz Vulf,

13:45.449 --> 13:48.369
I could have the opportunity to meet her?

13:48.452 --> 13:49.620
Yes.

13:49.703 --> 13:53.999
Well, it's not like I'm in a big rush,
so that can wait.

13:54.083 --> 13:59.547
More importantly, let's beat the Area Boss
right away and head to Fifticia, Psyger-0!

13:59.630 --> 14:02.758
The sun's gonna set on us
if we don't hurry!

14:02.841 --> 14:03.884
Um!

14:05.386 --> 14:11.016
Um, I have a favo-, no, a proposal.

14:11.100 --> 14:12.226
Yes?

14:12.309 --> 14:18.691
Well, calling me "Psyger-0" every time
seems to be quite a mouthful, isn't it?

14:19.275 --> 14:21.110
Well, I suppose.

14:21.193 --> 14:23.821
But then again,
if you just call me "Psyger,"

14:23.904 --> 14:27.366
it would get confusing with
my sis- err, Psyger-100.

14:27.449 --> 14:28.284
Yeah.

14:28.367 --> 14:30.911
S-So…!

14:30.995 --> 14:36.458
I-I-I think it would be easier
if you could call me "Rei" instead.

14:36.542 --> 14:38.043
Roger that.

14:38.127 --> 14:40.087
I'll go with "Rei," then.

14:43.090 --> 14:46.635
<i>Huh? Doesn't everyone just</i>
<i>call them "Psyger-0"?</i>

14:46.719 --> 14:48.596
<i>Was it "Psyger-Rei" all along?</i>

14:49.722 --> 14:54.226
<i>Rei? Zero? Psyger-Rei…</i>

14:54.310 --> 14:56.604
<i>It kinda rings a bell…</i>

14:57.980 --> 15:00.107
Hm? What's the matter, Rei?

15:00.733 --> 15:04.236
<i>H-H-H-He called me by my first name!</i>

15:05.237 --> 15:08.532
Are you all right, Rei? Rei?

15:08.616 --> 15:10.784
Thanks very much, Sunraku-san!

15:10.868 --> 15:12.411
I couldn't be better!

15:12.494 --> 15:14.997
I feel I can even beat Lycagon!

15:15.080 --> 15:17.166
Th-That's great…

15:17.249 --> 15:21.128
<i>I gotta help Hizutome-kun more</i>
<i>and close our distance!</i>

15:21.211 --> 15:26.175
Sunraku-san, there's actually
a shortcut towards the Area Boss.

15:26.258 --> 15:27.092
What?

15:27.176 --> 15:31.680
It's a slightly complex route, but if
you're in a rush, I'll show you the way!

15:31.764 --> 15:33.599
That'd be great!

15:33.682 --> 15:36.143
You sure know a lot, Rei!

15:38.646 --> 15:42.316
W-Well, I've been playing
this game for a year, so…

15:42.399 --> 15:46.654
Oh, so you're a veteran player!
I expect no less from you!

15:46.737 --> 15:48.113
No, uh…

15:48.197 --> 15:49.949
Oh, c'mon.

15:51.533 --> 15:53.535
<i>This seems to be going pretty well!</i>

15:54.578 --> 15:56.246
<i>To be honest,</i>

15:56.330 --> 16:03.295
<i>I want to work on that quest Vash-aniki</i>
<i>gave me that involves this place.</i>

16:03.879 --> 16:06.423
<i>But I guess I'll do it another time.</i>

16:07.675 --> 16:09.510
We'll go through this hole.

16:09.593 --> 16:10.970
Got it!

16:12.596 --> 16:18.102
<i>But Psyger-0, I mean, Rei.</i>
<i>I thought they were scary,</i>

16:18.185 --> 16:21.563
<i>but they're pretty easy to talk to,</i>
<i>and reliable, too.</i>

16:22.189 --> 16:24.566
<i>I'm so glad I invited them.</i>

16:25.317 --> 16:30.072
<i>Seems like I'll get to</i>
<i>Fifticia in time, no problem.</i>

16:40.666 --> 16:42.543
Um, Rei?

16:46.213 --> 16:47.089
Rei?

16:48.465 --> 16:51.427
The sun's down,
and the moon's out already.

16:51.510 --> 16:53.429
W-We're almost there!

16:53.512 --> 16:56.640
We're right near the Area Boss,
so don't worry!

16:56.724 --> 16:59.727
You said that around an hour ago.

17:01.520 --> 17:02.646
<i>I was trying to act cool</i>

17:02.730 --> 17:05.024
<i>and took him to a shortcut</i>
<i>I only remember vaguely,</i>

17:05.107 --> 17:07.234
<i>so now we're lost!</i>

17:10.154 --> 17:12.906
I've seen this wall before…

17:12.990 --> 17:15.534
<i>We're definitely lost…</i>

17:16.118 --> 17:20.039
<i>But what to do? This is the</i>
<i>Attack Master I'm dealing with.</i>

17:20.122 --> 17:25.252
<i>If I pointed that out and angered them,</i>
<i>they might chop me in four.</i>

17:25.335 --> 17:29.339
<i>They are giving me a hand,</i>
<i>so I guess I'll tag along a bit longer.</i>

17:33.677 --> 17:35.929
<i>As expected from the god-tier game SLF,</i>

17:36.013 --> 17:38.557
<i>they put great detail</i>
<i>on the night sky, too.</i>

17:39.600 --> 17:41.393
The moon is beautiful.

17:44.813 --> 17:48.317
Huh? Wh-What do you mean by that?

17:48.400 --> 17:49.234
Huh?

17:49.318 --> 17:54.573
W-Well, I heard Soseki Natsume
didn't actually say that.

17:54.656 --> 17:56.784
B-But, but!

17:56.867 --> 17:59.620
Sorry? Why are you
mentioning Soseki Natsume?

18:00.996 --> 18:02.081
Rei!

18:06.210 --> 18:07.961
That's a shamanistic spell!

18:08.045 --> 18:10.756
Oh my! I've seen your faces before.

18:16.053 --> 18:20.390
Apologies, but the road's
closed from here.

18:20.474 --> 18:24.228
Would you two mind taking
some other route?

18:25.437 --> 18:26.647
You…

18:26.730 --> 18:28.524
Animalia-san?

18:28.607 --> 18:32.778
It's an honor to have a top player
remember my name.

18:32.861 --> 18:35.989
Psyger-0-san, and Sunraku-san.

18:36.865 --> 18:41.286
What are you up to, dragging along
such a fully-armed members?

18:41.370 --> 18:43.914
Not up for some player-killing, I hope.

18:43.997 --> 18:45.791
Same goes for you.

18:45.874 --> 18:50.671
What are you up to this far away
from the exit at the edge of the area?

18:50.754 --> 18:53.257
What are we up to?
Beating this area, of course!

18:53.841 --> 18:56.760
Wait, edge of the area?

18:59.930 --> 19:03.809
<i>Could it be Rei severely lacks</i>
<i>a sense of direction?</i>

19:03.892 --> 19:07.604
In that case, I suppose this wasn't
a double booking after all.

19:08.355 --> 19:09.898
Double booking?

19:10.607 --> 19:13.819
Is there some event that
spawns here or something?

19:15.654 --> 19:18.448
If your goal is to beat the area,
turn back.

19:18.532 --> 19:21.326
You won't find the Area Boss here.

19:21.410 --> 19:28.292
I'm sure you realize just how unwise
it is to face off against all of us, right?

19:28.876 --> 19:31.253
You sure are acting intense.

19:31.336 --> 19:35.299
Are you angry because I took so long
to give you a reply on that Rabituza deal?

19:35.382 --> 19:37.259
Just give me more time.

19:37.342 --> 19:40.596
Oh, that. I'm cool now, thanks.

19:40.679 --> 19:43.015
Sorry, but you could
forget about that now.

19:44.349 --> 19:46.018
I'm not seeing what you're getting at.

19:47.936 --> 19:53.150
Your leader told me all 'bout
your secret after I paid off her debt.

19:54.026 --> 19:59.031
The condition to trigger the Unique
Scenario you so desperately tried to hide.

19:59.114 --> 20:02.284
Huh?! Pencilgon did what?!

20:02.367 --> 20:07.539
That depraved pencil! I'll break her spine
in half the next time I see her!

20:07.623 --> 20:12.127
"By landing a total of 100 critical hits
on Lycagon the Nightslayer,

20:12.211 --> 20:16.715
you will get an invite from Rabituza
which will trigger the Unique Scenario."

20:16.798 --> 20:18.008
Huh?

20:18.091 --> 20:23.180
<i>Wait, that alone wouldn't be enough</i>
<i>to trigger the Unique Scenario…</i>

20:23.263 --> 20:26.350
<i>I'll save up breaking</i>
<i>that pencil for later.</i>

20:26.433 --> 20:31.897
And after we complete that,
we can visit Rabituza whenever we like,

20:31.980 --> 20:35.525
and our dream will finally come true!

20:37.194 --> 20:40.864
<i>These guys don't even know</i>
<i>they just got fooled by Pencilgon.</i>

20:40.948 --> 20:42.866
<i>What an optimistic bunch.</i>

20:43.533 --> 20:45.118
I see.

20:45.202 --> 20:47.704
I get the situation now.

20:47.788 --> 20:49.873
But there's still something
I don't understand.

20:50.958 --> 20:53.627
Although already know all that,

20:53.710 --> 20:56.546
instead of hunting for
Lycagon the Nightslayer,

20:56.630 --> 21:02.427
why are you guarding this edge of the area
so badly to even want to fight for it?

21:15.941 --> 21:17.609
Wait, could it be…

21:18.151 --> 21:21.071
We are SF-Zoo.

21:21.154 --> 21:25.659
We will undertake any measure to
research every single detail

21:25.742 --> 21:31.123
about the lives and the behavior
patterns of monsters of our interest.

21:36.795 --> 21:43.135
In that one aspect,
we're above even the Library!

21:56.690 --> 22:03.447
Not even the Unique Monster,
Lycagon the Nightslayer…

22:05.324 --> 22:07.284
…is an exception!

22:22.841 --> 22:24.676
Can't stop trembling with excitement

22:24.760 --> 22:27.095
Ahhh it's the best feeling ever

22:27.179 --> 22:32.642
It's like when you end up laughing harder
the more you try to hold it in

22:32.726 --> 22:33.935
Well? What about you?

22:34.019 --> 22:37.022
Does your heartbeat throb
as it dances deep down inside?

22:37.105 --> 22:42.611
It's far more terrifying to contemplate a future
that ends without ever having known that feeling

22:42.694 --> 22:46.239
In a world filled with glitches

22:46.323 --> 22:51.828
Telling me not to glitch
is glitched out in itself, right?

22:52.537 --> 22:59.544
Same as ever,
we're still like hungry underdogs

23:00.545 --> 23:03.465
Step to the beat, to the beat

23:03.548 --> 23:05.675
It's a battered and bruised dance

23:05.759 --> 23:10.180
Barefoot and alone, I clench my teeth
and laugh as I kick at the rubble

23:10.263 --> 23:13.016
A paradise in an irreplaceable battlefield

23:13.100 --> 23:15.393
A stage with broken lighting fixture

23:15.477 --> 23:20.148
Suits this idiot perfectly

23:20.232 --> 23:23.527
The moon lights a path to the future

23:23.610 --> 23:27.739
Don't need to be told
I'm incorrigibly lame

23:27.823 --> 23:34.454
The incorrigibly lame-
they're the real deal
